cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this dataset or software, please cite it as below, and acknowledge NASA FIRMS as the source of the underlying active-fire detections."
title: "FireCal Harmonized Active Fire Record (MODIS→VIIRS)"
type: dataset
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-10-08"
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/sagoresarkerbdcse/nasa"
# TODO before the first release: list every team member (and ORCID iDs if you have them), e.g.
#   - family-names: "Sarker"
#     given-names: "..."
#     orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"
authors:
  - name: "FireCal AI team (NASA Space Apps Challenge 2026)"
keywords:
  - active fire
  - MODIS
  - VIIRS
  - NASA FIRMS
  - harmonization
  - climate data record
  - fire radiative power
  - biomass burning emissions
abstract: >-
  Monthly active-fire activity in VIIRS-equivalent fire-days for every country and every 1° cell,
  built from NASA FIRMS MODIS Collection 6.1 and VIIRS S-NPP 375 m archives. MODIS-only years are
  harmonized to VIIRS units with a season-stratified, hierarchically shrunk transfer and a small-fire
  floor, validated blind on held-out overlap years, with 90% intervals. Includes fire radiative energy
  and CO2/CO/PM2.5 emission estimates, a MODIS detection-probability model from same-overpass
  matchups, and a Terra/Aqua orbit-drift analysis.
references:
  - type: data
    title: "NASA Fire Information for Resource Management System (FIRMS)"
    authors:
      - name: "NASA Earth Science Data and Information System (ESDIS)"
    url: "https://www.earthdata.nasa.gov/data/tools/firms"
